===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} {{term|Ceres|Cerēs|lang=la}}, goddess of the bounty, akin to {{term|creare|crēare|to create|lang=la}}, {{term|crescere|crēscere|to grow|lang=la}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|ḱer-|to grow|lang=en}}. More at [[create]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɪəriːz/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{Roman god}} The Roman [[goddess]] of [[agriculture]]; equivalent to the [[Greek]] goddess [[Demeter]].  
# {{astronomy}} A celestial body [[orbit]]ing between [[Mars]] and [[Jupiter]], the largest [[asteroid]] and innermost [[dwarf planet]]; officially called {{term|1 Ceres|1 '''Ceres'''}}.

